<h5><b>International Center for Article Indexing and Evaluation</b></h5>
<br>International Library (IL) indexes and evaluates local and international articles and book. 

The International Library (IL) reviews and indexes books and articles from throughout the world. 
Once an article has been submitted for indexing in the International Library (IL), the process of assessment and indexing it begins. 
If accepted, it will also be indexed in 22 other partner online libraries. Publishers can also freely index all of the articles in their journal or magazine. 
The article will be assessed and its quality determined using 22 check list standards. 
Once the article has been indexed, an IL-Score will be generated based on a check list and shown on the article profile on the IL website. 
The article will be given a free International IOI Identifier (IOI), a modern DOI substitute that does not have the same issues as DOI. 
A special category code for the article will be assigned by the International Class Indetifier (ICI) and shown on the article profile.

